# Two-Site Refactor Safety

- Canonical plan: `docs/refactor/two-server/MASTER_PLAN.md`
- Machine order: `docs/refactor/two-server/execution-order.yaml`
- Execution governance: `docs/refactor/two-server/EXECUTION_GOVERNANCE.md`
- Standard non-external Stages have standing start authorization only after dependencies are complete.
- Execute one Stage per Worker; default to one writer and allow a second only with a Codex pairing receipt.
- Coordinator alone owns the integration branch and ledger; integrate candidates serially.
- Require one ACTIVE orchestrator fence whose platform/instance/epoch, integration head and
  Assignment/immutable-contract digest match before every mutation phase or commit; takeover
  requires clean registered worktrees and supersedes the old Assignment.
- Worker boundaries use read-only `worker-check`; only Coordinator runs `stage-advance`
  after the clean descendant commit and before verification.
- Require fenced `stage-open-check` before opening a Stage; unknown metadata and any
  production/destructive/DNS/Writer/secret flag block automatic continuation.
- Require success, failure, rollback and post-integration evidence.
- Deploy never changes DNS or Web Writer; only an explicit human dashboard action may do so.
- Finland is the sole Telegram Executor; SMS executes only on the current Web Writer/generation.
- Stop before production, migration/restore, real bucket mutation, secret access, DNS/Writer,
  destructive cleanup or legacy retirement unless Codex Final Reviewer authorized that exact action.
- Do not mark High/Critical gates green with fixtures, synthetic Market events, reset checkpoints
  or deleted evidence. Cursor cannot self-approve; an exact Codex Stage receipt plus patch-bound
  closeout receipt and post-commit verification are required before dependencies are released.
